WEBVTT

00:00.000 --> 00:06.000
The original request asks for a couch below a cup.
The first image puts the cup on the couch.

00:06.000 --> 00:12.000
Reflection raises the cup onto a shelf,
but the verifier no longer detects the couch.

00:12.000 --> 00:18.000
The next revision keeps the shelf and makes the couch explicit.
The resulting image passes verification.

00:18.000 --> 00:25.000
Reflection Skill Optimization learns when to intervene and how to revise.
For an unmet “below” relation, raise the upper object with physical support.
The skill guides the reflector with reusable conditions and actions.

00:25.000 --> 00:29.200
A skill-augmented reflector revises an on-policy failed rollout.
The verified revised prompt conditions the EMA teacher.

00:29.200 --> 00:35.000
At the same rollout state, the teacher evaluates original and revised prompts.
We extrapolate their velocity difference and match the student to this target,
while the student remains conditioned on the original prompt.

00:35.000 --> 00:42.000
After ReflectOPD training, the original prompt goes directly into the trained generator.
It hangs the backpack above the cat in one generation, with no external reflection loop.
No hook is specified in the prompt: the model adds one.
The small gray image shows the base model’s incorrect relation.
